---
/**
 * FAQ section: native <details>/<summary> accordions, no JS. Unnumbered
 * (sits between the toolbox grid and the final CTA).
 */
const base = import.meta.env.BASE_URL.replace(/\/$/, "");
const l = (path: string) => `${base}/${path}`;
---

<section class="section">
  <p class="section-eyebrow"><span class="t-dim">&gt;</span> faq</p>
  <h3 class="section-title rise">The questions we get first.</h3>

  <div class="faq rise">
    <details>
      <summary>Is the AI mandatory?</summary>
      <p>
        No. Without authenticating the <code>claude</code> CLI, Stubwise is a
        complete self-hosted issue tracker: ingestion, board, comments,
        milestones all work. AI jobs just stay queued.
      </p>
    </details>
    <details>
      <summary>Which AI does it use?</summary>
      <p>
        The worker drives the Claude Code CLI. You authenticate with an API key
        or a Claude subscription login, and can configure an
        <a href={l("getting-started/claude-setup/")}>ordered chain of
        credentials</a> with failover. Models are configurable per phase
        (planning vs execution).
      </p>
    </details>
    <details>
      <summary>Does my code leave my server?</summary>
      <p>
        Only where you point it: your git provider and your AI provider, with
        your credentials. Search, embeddings, docs and knowledge graphs are
        computed and stored on your host.
      </p>
    </details>
    <details>
      <summary>What does it take to run?</summary>
      <p>
        Docker Compose, one <code>.env</code>, six containers. Migrations apply
        themselves on startup; the embedding model is a one-time
        <code>ollama pull</code>. See the
        <a href={l("getting-started/self-hosting/")}>self-hosting guide</a>.
      </p>
    </details>
    <details>
      <summary>Which git providers are supported?</summary>
      <p>
        GitHub and Bitbucket Cloud, behind a <code>GitProvider</code> interface
        designed to be extended — adding one is a documented contribution path.
      </p>
    </details>
    <details>
      <summary>How does it relate to Claude Code?</summary>
      <p>
        Twice over: the worker <em>uses</em> the Claude Code CLI to do its
        jobs, and the <code>@stubwise/mcp</code> server lets Claude Code
        <em>drive</em> Stubwise — backlog, designs, plans and tickets — from
        your <a href={l("integrations/claude-code-mcp/")}>coding session</a>.
      </p>
    </details>
  </div>
</section>

<style>
  .faq {
    max-width: 52rem;
  }
  .faq details {
    border: 1px solid var(--border);
    background: var(--panel);
    margin-bottom: 0.6rem;
    transition: border-color 0.2s ease;
  }
  .faq details:hover,
  .faq details[open] {
    border-color: var(--amber);
  }
  .faq summary {
    display: flex;
    align-items: center;
    justify-content: space-between;
    gap: 1rem;
    padding: 0.95rem 1.2rem;
    cursor: pointer;
    list-style: none;
    font-size: 0.92rem;
    font-weight: 600;
    color: var(--text);
  }
  .faq summary::-webkit-details-marker {
    display: none;
  }
  .faq summary::marker {
    content: none;
  }
  /* Starlight styles .sl-markdown-content details with a ::before caret. */
  .faq summary::before {
    display: none;
  }
  .faq summary::after {
    content: "+";
    flex: none;
    font-weight: 700;
    color: var(--amber);
  }
  .faq details[open] summary::after {
    content: "×";
  }
  .faq details p {
    margin: 0;
    padding: 0 1.2rem 1.05rem;
    font-size: 0.85rem;
    line-height: 1.7;
    color: var(--dim);
  }
  .faq details code {
    color: var(--amber);
    background: none;
  }
</style>
